{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>A gift</b>, <b>of a righteous man</b> — [verses 16–17] two joined units." "<b>And a gift</b> — an allusion to a bribe that one gives; it brings him out into broad space from his straits." "<b>and before great men it will set him</b> — these are takers of bribe, so that he does not fail before them in judgment."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:31.597452076Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}